<!--
  Entitlements of the app, signed into it by scripts/sign-app.sh. Empty on purpose.
  Every key added here needs a comment with its documented reason.

  - No com.apple.security.app-sandbox: the app is not sandboxed.
  - No com.apple.security.device.audio-input. Apple documents it as the hardened runtime entitlement to
    "record audio using the built-in microphone and access audio input using Core Audio". Apple's article
    "Capturing system audio with Core Audio taps" names only NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription in Info.plist
    and the system audio recording prompt for a tap, and no entitlement. Not verified: whether reading the
    aggregate device that holds the tap counts as audio input under the hardened runtime. Release 0.1.0
    already ran with the hardened runtime and without this key, so this file changes nothing there.
    Add the key only after a signed build is measured to stay silent without it.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
